From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Navmesh tiles removed under a running query

dtNavMesh::removeTile zeroes tile->polys, and dtNavMeshQuery reaches for it
through getTileAndPolyByRefUnsafe, which by design validates nothing. Any
polyRef that outlives the removal therefore resolves to nullptr + index.

That is not a theory. Two crashes on 2026-08-05, both inside
dtQueryFilter::passFilter reached from PathInfo::BuildPolyPath, with poly at
0x2fce0 and 0x2cca0 - 195808 and 183456, both exact multiples of
sizeof(dtPoly) = 32, so polygon indices 6119 and 5733 counted from a null
base.

The tiles are removed by TerrainInfo::CleanUpGrids every GridCleanUpDelay
milliseconds. Worth knowing: that function never looks at GridUnload. The
config governs object grids, not terrain, so setting it to 0 does not stop
navmesh tiles from being unloaded - which is what sent us looking in the
wrong place first.

A read/write lock around the mesh was the obvious answer and it is the wrong
one. Tried and reverted: PathInfo::calculate holds it for the whole call and
Map::GetWalkHitPosition takes the same lock underneath, so as soon as a
writer queues up, glibc stops admitting readers and the world thread stalls.
Not a crash, a silent freeze, which is worse.

Keeping the tile loaded removes the problem instead of racing it. Nothing is
ever zeroed, so no reference can go stale. It costs memory - on a server
where bots roam everywhere, the tiles were largely staying loaded anyway -
and MMapTileUnload = 1 restores the old behaviour without a rebuild.

Applies to any mangos-family tree; nothing here is playerbot specific,
though a thousand of them is what made it show up daily rather than yearly.
---
diff --git a/src/game/Maps/MoveMap.cpp b/src/game/Maps/MoveMap.cpp
index b9045f2..e00b971 100644
--- a/src/game/Maps/MoveMap.cpp
+++ b/src/game/Maps/MoveMap.cpp
@@ -207,6 +207,15 @@ bool MMapManager::loadMap(uint32 mapId, int32 x, int32 y)
 
 bool MMapManager::unloadMap(uint32 mapId, int32 x, int32 y)
 {
+    // dtNavMesh::removeTile zeroes tile->polys, and getTileAndPolyByRefUnsafe
+    // reads it without validating: any polyRef that outlives the removal
+    // resolves to nullptr + index. Keeping the tile loaded makes that
+    // impossible, and costs less than locking queries against cleanup.
+    // Crashes of 2026-08-05: poly was 0x2fce0 and 0x2cca0, both exact
+    // multiples of sizeof(dtPoly) = 32.
+    if (!sWorld.getConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_MMAP_TILE_UNLOAD))
+        return false;
+
     // check if we have this map loaded
     if (loadedMMaps.find(mapId) == loadedMMaps.end())
     {
@@ -250,6 +259,12 @@ bool MMapManager::unloadMap(uint32 mapId, int32 x, int32 y)
 
 bool MMapManager::unloadMap(uint32 mapId)
 {
+    // Same reason as above, plus: MMapData is keyed by mapId, not by
+    // instance. Tearing down one instance while a second one of the same
+    // map is running would pull the mesh out from under it.
+    if (!sWorld.getConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_MMAP_TILE_UNLOAD))
+        return false;
+
     if (loadedMMaps.find(mapId) == loadedMMaps.end())
     {
         // file may not exist, therefore not loaded
diff --git a/src/game/World.cpp b/src/game/World.cpp
index be94fb0..5d01ee2 100644
--- a/src/game/World.cpp
+++ b/src/game/World.cpp
@@ -1031,6 +1031,7 @@ void World::LoadConfigSettingsFromFile(bool reload)
     setConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_CLEAN_CHARACTER_DB, "CleanCharacterDB", true);
     setConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_GRID_UNLOAD, "GridUnload", true);
     setConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_CLEANUP_TERRAIN, "CleanupTerrain", true);
+    setConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_MMAP_TILE_UNLOAD, "MMapTileUnload", false);
     setConfigPos(CONFIG_UINT32_INTERVAL_SAVE, "PlayerSave.Interval", 15 * MINUTE * IN_MILLISECONDS);
     setConfigMinMax(CONFIG_UINT32_MIN_LEVEL_STAT_SAVE, "PlayerSave.Stats.MinLevel", 0, 0, MAX_LEVEL);
     setConfig(CONFIG_BOOL_STATS_SAVE_ONLY_ON_LOGOUT, "PlayerSave.Stats.SaveOnlyOnLogout", true);
diff --git a/src/game/World.h b/src/game/World.h
index 8af4c9c..7e460c0 100644
--- a/src/game/World.h
+++ b/src/game/World.h
@@ -736,6 +736,9 @@ enum eConfigBoolValues
     // See LFT/LFTBotFill.cpp
     CONFIG_BOOL_LFT_BOTFILL_ENABLE,
     CONFIG_BOOL_AUTOSCALER_ENABLE,
+    // Remove navmesh tiles again at runtime. Off by default, see
+    // MMapManager::unloadMap.
+    CONFIG_BOOL_MMAP_TILE_UNLOAD,
     CONFIG_BOOL_VALUE_COUNT
 };
 
@@ -1365,7 +1368,7 @@ class World
         // Login-Zeitpunkte nicht auf einen gemeinsamen Takt synchronisiert
         // werden muessen (jeder Account bekommt seine eigene volle Stunde).
         std::unordered_map<uint32 /*accountId*/, uint32 /*accumulatedMs*/> m_donationPointAccumulatorMs;
-        // Wie lange bis zum naechsten periodischen Persistieren der obigen
+        // Time until the next periodic persist of the above
         // Akkumulatoren nach `donation_point_progress` (Login-DB) - siehe
         // World.cpp. Ohne Persistenz fing der Fortschritt nach jedem Neustart
         // wieder bei 0 an.
diff --git a/src/mangosd/mangosd.conf.dist.in b/src/mangosd/mangosd.conf.dist.in
index e903d37..08b0927 100644
--- a/src/mangosd/mangosd.conf.dist.in
+++ b/src/mangosd/mangosd.conf.dist.in
@@ -152,6 +152,17 @@ GridUnload = 0
 
 CleanupTerrain = 1
 
+#    MMapTileUnload
+#        Remove navmesh tiles from the mesh again at runtime.
+#        dtNavMesh::removeTile zeroes tile->polys, and dtNavMeshQuery reads it
+#        through getTileAndPolyByRefUnsafe without validating - any polyRef
+#        that outlives the removal resolves to nullptr + index and takes the
+#        server down. Left off, tiles stay loaded: that costs memory but
+#        cannot go wrong.
+#        Default: 0 (off)
+
+MMapTileUnload = 0
+
 # GridCleanUpDelay. Grid clean up delay.
 
 GridCleanUpDelay = 300000
-- 
2.43.0

